---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { buildFAQSchema } from "../lib/seo";

const faqSections = [
  {
    title: "About the lessons",
    intro: "Use the free lessons when you want a clear explanation first and teacher support second.",
    items: [
      {
        question: "Are the lessons really free?",
        answer: "Yes. The lessons are free to read on the site. Paid support is only for students who want direct help such as tutoring, essay correction, or the writing score lab.",
        body: "<p>Yes. The lessons are free to read on the site. Paid support is only for students who want direct help such as tutoring, essay correction, or the writing score lab.</p>",
      },
      {
        question: "Where should I start if I feel lost?",
        answer: "Start with the one skill that is lowering your score most. Do not try to fix everything in one day.",
        body: "<p>Start with the one skill that is lowering your score most. If writing is weak, start with writing. If grammar errors keep appearing, start with one grammar point. The best first step is usually one focused lesson, not five random ones.</p>",
      },
      {
        question: "How many lessons are there?",
        answer: "There are hundreds of lessons across grammar, vocabulary, writing, and speaking.",
        body: "<p>There are hundreds of lessons across grammar, vocabulary, writing, and speaking. The goal is not to read everything. The goal is to find the lesson that fixes the problem you have right now.</p>",
      },
      {
        question: "How long is each lesson?",
        answer: "Most lessons take about 5 to 15 minutes to read, depending on the topic.",
        body: "<p>Most lessons take about 5 to 15 minutes to read, depending on the topic. The stronger approach is to read one lesson carefully, do the interactive task, and only then move to the next page.</p>",
      },
      {
        question: "Are lessons for IELTS or CELPIP?",
        answer: "Both. Many lessons help both exams because the underlying English skill is the same, while some pages are task-specific.",
        body: "<p>Both. Many lessons help both exams because grammar, vocabulary, and sentence control overlap. Some pages are task-specific when the format changes, such as IELTS Writing Task 2 or CELPIP Writing Task 1.</p>",
      },
      {
        question: "What level do the lessons cover?",
        answer: "The site covers beginner to advanced levels, but the explanations are written to stay understandable even when the topic is harder.",
        body: "<p>The site covers beginner to advanced levels. Even when the grammar point is B2 or C1, the explanation should still be readable for a lower-intermediate learner.</p>",
      },
      {
        question: "Can I download the lessons?",
        answer: "Not yet. Right now the lessons are designed for online study.",
        body: "<p>Not yet. Right now the lessons are designed for online study on phone or desktop. If downloadable versions are added later, they will be announced on the site and through the newsletter.</p>",
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "About tutoring",
    intro: "Use tutoring when you need direct feedback, speaking practice, or a study plan for a real deadline.",
    items: [
      {
        question: "How much does tutoring cost?",
        answer: "Tutoring is CA$30 for a 60-minute one-to-one lesson.",
        body: "<p><strong>CA$30 for a 60-minute one-to-one lesson.</strong> The lesson is live and focused on the exam skill or score problem you want to fix.</p>",
      },
      {
        question: "What happens after I contact you?",
        answer: "You explain your exam and goal, we reply with a suitable next step, and then you choose whether to book.",
        body: "<ol><li>You send your exam, level, and target.</li><li>We reply with the most suitable next step.</li><li>If tutoring is the right fit, we offer times and booking details.</li></ol>",
      },
      {
        question: "What can we work on in tutoring?",
        answer: "Tutoring can focus on speaking, writing, grammar, strategy, or a full study plan.",
        body: "<ul><li><strong>Writing:</strong> structure, task response, sentence control, and rewriting</li><li><strong>Speaking:</strong> mock tests, fluency, pronunciation, and answer building</li><li><strong>Grammar:</strong> targeted explanation of repeated mistakes</li><li><strong>Strategy:</strong> timing, question handling, and study planning</li></ul>",
      },
      {
        question: "Can you guarantee a score?",
        answer: "No. No honest teacher can guarantee a score. What can be done is to diagnose the weak skill and help you improve it clearly.",
        body: "<p>No. No honest teacher can guarantee a score. Test results still depend on your current level, the time you have, your practice habits, and how you perform on the day. What we can do is identify the weak skill and work on it directly.</p>",
      },
      {
        question: "How many sessions do students usually need?",
        answer: "That depends on the gap between your current score and target score.",
        body: "<p>That depends on the gap between your current score and target score. Some students need a few focused sessions for writing or speaking. Others need a longer plan. The first conversation usually makes that much clearer.</p>",
      },
      {
        question: "Do you offer group lessons?",
        answer: "Sometimes, if a small group has the same goal and level.",
        body: "<p>Sometimes. If a small group has a similar level and a similar target, contact us and ask. One-to-one teaching is still the main format because it gives better feedback.</p>",
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "About writing feedback",
    intro: "Use writing feedback when you already practice on your own but still do not know why the score stays low.",
    items: [
      {
        question: "How much does essay correction cost?",
        answer: "Essay correction is CA$15 per piece.",
        body: "<p><strong>CA$15 per piece.</strong> That is for direct feedback on your writing, not a generic score label.</p>",
      },
      {
        question: "How long does it take to get feedback?",
        answer: "Usually 24 to 48 hours, and sometimes up to 72 hours during busier periods.",
        body: "<p>Usually 24 to 48 hours, and sometimes up to 72 hours during busier periods. If your exam is close, mention the date in your message.</p>",
      },
      {
        question: "What kind of feedback do I get?",
        answer: "You get comments on grammar, vocabulary, organization, and the main issues that are hurting the score.",
        body: "<ul><li>Grammar and vocabulary corrections</li><li>Comments on organization and task response</li><li>An estimated score range</li><li>The main mistakes to fix next</li><li>Practical guidance for the next rewrite</li></ul>",
      },
      {
        question: "Can you mark letters and emails too?",
        answer: "Yes. IELTS Task 1 letters, CELPIP emails, and similar writing tasks can all be reviewed.",
        body: "<p>Yes. IELTS Task 1 letters, CELPIP emails, survey responses, and similar writing tasks can all be reviewed.</p>",
      },
      {
        question: "How is the writing score lab different from essay correction?",
        answer: "The writing score lab is a subscription tool for faster repeated checks. Essay correction is a more direct reviewed service for individual pieces.",
        body: "<p>The writing score lab is better when you want ongoing practice and quick repeated checks. Essay correction is better when you want more direct attention on one piece of writing.</p>",
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "General questions",
    intro: "These are the questions people ask when they want to know how the site works overall.",
    items: [
      {
        question: "Who is IELTS Corner for?",
        answer: "The site is for IELTS and CELPIP students who want clearer teaching, stronger writing and speaking, or a more focused study plan.",
        body: "<p>The site is for IELTS and CELPIP students who want clearer teaching, stronger writing and speaking, or a more focused study plan. Some people only use the free lessons. Others add tutoring or writing feedback when they need direct help.</p>",
      },
      {
        question: "How do payments work?",
        answer: "Payment details are shared once the service is confirmed. Current options include Stripe, PayPal, and e-transfer where appropriate.",
        body: "<p>Payment details are shared once the service is confirmed. Current options include Stripe, PayPal, and e-transfer where appropriate.</p>",
      },
      {
        question: "What if a service is not the right fit?",
        answer: "Tell us quickly. The goal is to solve the problem directly, not make support frustrating.",
        body: "<p>Tell us quickly. The goal is to solve the problem directly, not make support frustrating. More detailed policy information is available in the <a href=\"/terms\">terms of service</a>.</p>",
      },
      {
        question: "Is there a privacy policy?",
        answer: "Yes. The privacy policy explains what data is collected and how it is used.",
        body: "<p>Yes. The <a href=\"/privacy\">privacy policy</a> explains what data is collected and how it is used.</p>",
      },
      {
        question: "Still have a specific question?",
        answer: "Use the contact page and include your exam, current level, and target.",
        body: "<p><a href=\"/contact\">Use the contact page</a> and include your exam, current level, and target. That usually leads to a much more useful reply.</p>",
      },
    ],
  },
];

const faqStructuredData = [
  buildFAQSchema(
    faqSections.flatMap((section) => (
      section.items.map((item) => ({
        question: item.question,
        answer: item.answer,
      }))
    )),
  ),
];

const quickRoutes = [
  {
    title: "Use free lessons",
    text: "Best when you want to study one topic on your own first.",
    href: "/lessons",
    label: "Open lessons",
  },
  {
    title: "Use tutoring",
    text: "Best when your test date is close and you need direct guidance.",
    href: "/tutoring",
    label: "See tutoring",
  },
  {
    title: "Use writing feedback",
    text: "Best when your essays or emails keep losing marks and you do not know why.",
    href: "/essay-correction",
    label: "See writing feedback",
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="FAQ | IELTS Corner"
  description="Frequently asked questions about IELTS Corner lessons, tutoring, writing feedback, and study support."
  type="page"
  structuredData={faqStructuredData}
>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: var(--s-6);">
    <div class="hero" style={`--hero-bg: url('/heroes/faq.png');`}>
      <div class="hero-content">
        <h1>Frequently asked questions</h1>
        <p>
          Use this page when you want the short answer first. If your question is more specific,
          the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> is the better next step.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="height: var(--s-6);"></div>

    <div class="grid grid-3 faq-routes">
      {quickRoutes.map((route) => (
        <article class="surface faq-route-card">
          <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">{route.title}</h2>
          <p>{route.text}</p>
          <a href={route.href} class="btn btn-ghost">{route.label}</a>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div style="height: var(--s-6);"></div>

    <div class="stack" style="gap: var(--s-6);">
      {faqSections.map((section) => (
        <section>
          <h2>{section.title}</h2>
          <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 0; max-width: 72ch;">{section.intro}</p>

          <div class="faq-group">
            {section.items.map((item) => (
              <details class="faq-item">
                <summary class="faq-summary">{item.question}</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer" set:html={item.body}></div>
              </details>
            ))}
          </div>
        </section>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div style="height: var(--s-7);"></div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .faq-routes {
    gap: var(--s-3);
  }

  .faq-route-card {
    padding: var(--s-4);
    border-radius: 16px;
  }

  .faq-group {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-2);
  }

  .faq-item {
    all: revert;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: 14px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .faq-summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .faq-summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-summary::after {
    content: "+";
    float: right;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .faq-item[open] .faq-summary {
    background: var(--accent-light);
  }

  .faq-item[open] .faq-summary::after {
    content: "-";
  }

  .faq-answer {
    padding: 0 1.1rem 1.1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .faq-answer :global(p:first-child) {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .faq-routes {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr !important;
    }
  }
</style>
